#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Sentinel GT AI — one local file for a human-in-the-loop Tier 2 engineer.

Drop a historian CSV, the analytic name and your notes. The app drafts a site report
with evidence. You review it, correct it, and teach the app. Retrain stays on this computer.
Review and inference do not use the network. ``setup`` is the only command that downloads.

    python sentinel_gt_ai.py setup
    python sentinel_gt_ai.py
    python sentinel_gt_ai.py doctor
    python sentinel_gt_ai.py train --quick --device auto

The blocks under each banner are the package modules, comments included. They sit in
``if False`` so this file stays valid Python; the loader compiles each block into the
``sentinel.*`` module it came from. Edit a block in place. Data stays outside the file:
models/, knowledge/, data/, settings.local.json.

TABLE OF CONTENTS
  303  sentinel — Package identity: version and app name. Submodules hang off this.
  315  sentinel.config — CONFIG — every tunable setting. Defaults live on class Settings. settings.local.json and SENTINEL_* environment variables override them. Nothing here contacts the network.
 1000  sentinel.limits — Fixed engineering thresholds the rule path compares sensor readings against.
 1089  sentinel.notes — Pull unit id, first-out text and free-text hints out of the engineer's notes.
 1213  sentinel.charts — Evidence charts and the residual view. Altair keeps the heatmap contract; the UI plots use plotly (matplotlib, then Altair) with one local palette. No remote assets.
 1597  sentinel.e2e — Learned path package marker.
 1608  sentinel.e2e.labels — Engineer labels, metric log, and the version folder (v0000 is the shipped head).
 2125  sentinel.e2e.evaluation — Cached rule-path scores and the confusion tables the eval report uses.
 2224  sentinel.e2e.dashboard — Learning-dashboard series: held-out accuracy, rolling agreement, label counts.
 2342  sentinel.data — Read a historian CSV into canonical roles. Ring and zone tags sort by full sensor number; each frame model points at a tag layout.
 2744  sentinel.profiles — Tag profiles: schema, loader and validation. One JSON file per alert type. A bad file is skipped.
 4653  sentinel.knowledge — Retrieve process-map sections for the prompt. Learned 'why' notes from Teach sit beside the shipped maps.
 5020  sentinel.rules — Shadow rule names the learned path stores next to its own decision.
 5069  sentinel.llm_runtime — The one LLM: Gemma 4 12B Q4_K_M. GPU offload when it loads, else CPU, else the template.
 5455  sentinel.e2e.train_job — Retrain in a subprocess so a Streamlit rerun does not kill it. Progress lives in data/e2e/jobs.
 5680  sentinel.bootstrap — setup: venv, pinned installs, model download or --models-from, starter knowledge, optional train.
 6231  sentinel.analytics.base — Shared evidence types and the robust statistics every analyzer uses.
 6475  sentinel.e2e.features — Canonical 14-channel window (512 points) the encoder was fine-tuned on. Do not reorder it.
 7183  sentinel.analytics.cold_spot — Rule-path cold-sector check: a contiguous arc of the exhaust ring, not one noisy thermocouple.
 7570  sentinel.analytics.combustion_dynamics — Rule-path dynamics check: pulsation that is real versus a dead probe.
 7955  sentinel.analytics.hets_trip — Rule-path trip check: first-out spread trip versus a sensor step that only looks like one.
 8335  sentinel.analytics.generic — Fallback when the analytic name matches no dedicated rule set. It still reports evidence and asks for a human.
 8452  sentinel.anomaly — Rule-path anomaly scan: robust z always, TS Pulse reconstruction when that snapshot loads.
 8678  sentinel.report — Deterministic template narrative. Used when the LLM is off, missing, or fails its checks.
 8938  sentinel.store — Cases, feedback and the review gate, as files under data/. No database.
 9249  sentinel.llm — Prompt and JSON schema for the rule-path narrative, plus the number check on the model's reply.
 9494  sentinel.e2e.taxonomy — Signature ids the head can name, plus NOVEL, which is never trained as a class.
 9796  sentinel.e2e.encoder — TS Pulse fine-tune and embed. device auto|gpu|cpu, and a CPU retry when the GPU runs out of memory.
10678  sentinel.e2e.residual — Second TS Pulse view: reconstruction residual, robust-z fallback, cross-check against the classifier.
12253  sentinel.analytics — Resolve the free-text analytic name Tier 1 typed to one analyzer.
12411  sentinel.e2e.model — Light head, similarity index and novelty calibration on frozen embeddings.
13727  sentinel.e2e.dataset — Load the synthetic manifest and import or export engineer-labeled CSV folders.
14041  sentinel.e2e.report — Markdown site report for a learned-path case, including the residual evidence rows.
14471  sentinel.e2e.teach — Teach the app: labeled cases with a why, process documents, signatures, version rollback.
15423  sentinel.cli — Command line: run, doctor, train, setup, and the NiceGUI launcher.
16295  sentinel.generator — Built-in synthetic historian CSVs. setup --train uses these when the encoder is missing.
17931  sentinel.triage — Turn analyzer findings into one action, an urgency and the reasons a human must look.
18180  sentinel.e2e.train — Quick-update pieces: refit the head, recalibrate novelty, score held-out, promote only when not worse.
20546  sentinel.e2e.migrate — Assign stored labels and cases to alert-type profiles. The legacy label log, embeddings and registry are not rewritten.
21418  sentinel.e2e.writer — What the LLM sees on the learned path: evidence, residual, process steps, and the cross-check.
21904  sentinel.e2e.simulate — Site-adaptation drill used by tests: label, retrain the head, measure the lift.
22020  sentinel.ui — NiceGUI pages: header tabs, black and mint theme. serve() starts the server; importing this module does not.
24102  sentinel.pipeline — Rule path end to end: CSV, notes, analyzer, triage, template or LLM, save.
24291  sentinel.e2e.engine — Load one version (head, and the encoder that version belongs to) and run decide.
25203  sentinel.e2e.pipeline — Learned path end to end: features, decide, rules in shadow, report, save.
"""

